# Commits that changed only whitespace, and that `git blame` should look straight through.
#
# GitHub honours this file automatically. Locally it needs one opt-in, once:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Only ever add a commit here that is PROVABLY whitespace-only — the proof this project
# accepts is `git diff -w --stat <sha>^ <sha>` printing nothing while `git diff --stat`
# prints a large number. A commit listed here becomes invisible to blame, so a real change
# hidden in one is a real change nobody can attribute.

